TXT ============================================================;
TXT Example: Roof battens (Dachlatten) with pitch-adjusted nailing;
TXT NR rotation: ry to follow roof pitch (30°), so nails penetrate;
TXT perpendicular to the underlying rafter surface;
TXT Use case: Roof construction, battens on sarking board;
TXT NOTE: rx/ry/rz parameters require consultation with WEINMANN;
TXT ============================================================;
VERSION 3.8;
ELEMENTID b1a2c3d4-1002-4000-8002-000000000002;
ANR Example-NR-Rotation-2026;
ELB ROOF-BATTEN-RY;
ELN ex-rb-ry-002;
ZNR 0002;
TXT Element: roof panel 4000mm x 3200mm, slope 30°, build-up 100mm;
ELM 4000,3200,100,1;
CAD wupEditor;
CADRELEASE 2026.08;
BEARBEITER WEINMANN Example;
BAUVORHABEN NR Rotation Examples;

TXT --- Rafters (LS) running in X direction, spacing 800mm ---;
TXT Rafter 1;
LS 4000,60,180,0,0,0,rafter-1,0;
TXT Rafter 2;
LS 4000,60,180,0,800,0,rafter-2,0;
TXT Rafter 3;
LS 4000,60,180,0,1600,0,rafter-3,0;
TXT Rafter 4;
LS 4000,60,180,0,2400,0,rafter-4,0;
TXT Rafter 5;
LS 4000,60,180,0,3140,0,rafter-5,0;

TXT --- Sarking board (Schalungsbrett) PLI1 on top of rafters ---;
PLI1 4000,3200,24,0,0,3,sarking-board,0;
PP 0,0,24,0,0,0;
PP 4000,0,24,0,0,0;
PP 4000,3200,24,0,0,0;
PP 0,3200,24,0,0,0;
PP 0,0,24,0,0,0;

TXT --- Roof battens (Dachlatten) 40x60mm perpendicular to rafters ---;
TXT Battens run in Y direction, nailed through sarking board into rafters;
TXT ry=30° tilts nail to match the 30° roof pitch projection;
TXT so nail enters the rafter at a right angle to its sloped surface;

TXT Batten 1 at x=400 (between edge and first rafter);
PLI2 40,3200,60,400,0,3,roof-batten-1,0;
PP 400,0,60,0,0,0;
PP 440,0,60,0,0,0;
PP 440,3200,60,0,0,0;
PP 400,3200,60,0,0,0;
PP 400,0,60,0,0,0;
TXT Nail line - ry=30 tilts nail by 30° around Y axis (roof pitch angle);
NR 420,100,420,3100,400,10,0,30,0;

